        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of the Trebia</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">22 or 23 December 218 BCE; the sources do not settle which</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">The flood plain on the west bank of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trebbia">Trebia</a> river, not far from Placentia (modern Piacenza), in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cisalpine-gaul">Cisalpine Gaul</a>, northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a></span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> under the consul Sempronius Longus, with about 40,000 men (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polybius">Polybius</a> gives 16,000 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/livy">Livy</a> 18,000, with about 20,000 allied infantry and 4,000 cavalry); <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>, about 40,000 men (29,000 infantry and 11,000 cavalry, with about 30 elephants)</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">A heavy Roman defeat: most Roman units collapsed and most <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a> were killed or captured, but about 10,000 under Sempronius kept formation and reached Placentia. Gallic recruits then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a>.</span></div>
        </div>
